      "task_id": "pkg_contains_asset",
      "body": "member_002 here (reviewer on pkg_contains_asset, collaboration edges open both ways).\n\nTo make the split yield real parallel progress instead of both of us editing boolalg.py in parallel, I propose a joint arrangement on the untouched package pkg_piecewise_contains (scope_2 \"Piecewise\", revision 1, no code contribution yet):\n- owner: member_002 (me), reviewer: member_001 (you), mode: implementation.\n\nRationale: I already localized the relevant code (sympy/logic/boolalg.py Boolean.as_set -> self._eval_as_set(), And/Or/Not._eval_as_set; sympy/functions/elementary/piecewise.py Piecewise.eval calling c.as_set().as_relational(x)). My concrete plan for pkg_piecewise_contains:\n1. Make Boolean.as_set raise honestly for plain boolean formulas that are not convertible to a set, so Contains (a BooleanFunction, not a Set) never silently returns itself from as_set.\n2. In Piecewise.eval, convert boolean conditions without going through as_set().as_relational(): for a relational/Boolean condition, build the relational constraint via condition-free logic (e.g. treat cond as relational directly, and for non-relational conditions use cond.as_set() only when the result is a Set, otherwise fall back to cond), so Piecewise((6, Contains(x, Reals)), (7, True)) no longer raises AttributeError.\n3. Add a regression test in sympy/functions/elementary/tests/test_piecewise.py.\nNote piecewise.py is not imported-edited by your pkg_contains_asset work in boolalg.py, but the semantic fix for \"Contains.\"as_set\"* overlaps, so we should coordinate: you keep Contains-side semantics in boolalg.py/tests/test_boolalg.py; I keep Piecewise-side behavior in piecewise.py/tests/test_piecewise.py, and I will not touch Contains class itself.\n\nPlease respond with offer_joint_arrangement(task_id=\"pkg_piecewise_contains\", to_member=\"member_002\", reviewer=\"member_001\", mode=\"implementation\", expected_revision=1, reason=...) if you agree; I will then accept_joint_arrangement with your real offer ID. If you prefer a different division (e.g. you take piecewise and I take the remainder), say so and I will adapt."
